# Default owner for everything.
* @sethcarney

# CODEOWNERS is what turns "Require a pull request before merging" into
# "require a review from someone who knows this file". On its own the file only
# requests reviewers; it is binding once "Require review from Code Owners" is
# ticked in the branch protection rule (docs/supply-chain.md#github-side-setup).
#
# The paths below are called out separately because they are the ones where a
# wrong change is a security bug rather than a broken feature. On a
# single-maintainer repo they resolve to the same person as the default rule —
# they earn their place the day a second contributor arrives, and cost nothing
# until then.

# Anything that builds a command line, a URI, or a spawn argv. The quoting in
# terminal/command.ts is a security boundary, and editor/uri.ts must not
# normalise the host path (see CLAUDE.md, "the raw label rule").
/src/main/terminal/    @sethcarney
/src/main/editor/      @sethcarney

# The Electron hardening: webPreferences, CSP, permission handlers, the
# external-origin allow-list, and IPC sender validation.
/src/main/index.ts     @sethcarney
/src/preload/          @sethcarney
/src/shared/ipc.ts     @sethcarney

# The environment rule: mapContainer reads exactly one variable out of
# Config.Env and must never let the rest reach a snapshot or a log.
/src/main/docker/      @sethcarney

# CI, release, signing, and the supply-chain posture itself. A workflow change
# is a change to what runs with this repo's token.
/.github/              @sethcarney
/SECURITY.md           @sethcarney
/docs/supply-chain.md  @sethcarney
/docs/electron-security.md @sethcarney
